title: PyCon DE 2027 Tickets
---
intro:

> Ticket sales are open. Limited: 1,400 seats for three days on site.
---
body:

## Four editions

Every three-day pass belongs to an edition. The edition says when you joined the year.
Prices in EUR, incl. VAT.

| | Edition I: Early Bird | Edition II: Blind Bird | Edition III: Wise Bird | Edition IV: Late Bird |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| On sale | 21 October 12:00 CEST, 150 tickets | when Edition I is gone, 4 November at the latest, until 10 February | 10 February, speakers announced, until 3 March | 3 March, schedule published, until sold out |
| **Standard**<br><small>business expense: company, start-up, public sector or freelancer</small> | 690 € | 790 € | 890 € | 990 € |
| **Self-funded**<br><small>personal: your own pocket, or researcher at a public academic institution</small> | 450 € | 500 € | 550 € | 625 € |
| **Student**<br><small>personal: full-time with a valid student ID at the conference, whoever pays</small> | 275 € | 300 € | 325 € | 375 € |

Once an edition closes, it never reopens. Each pass includes the limited shirt of its edition.

## Remote tickets and day passes

Remote: all talks live and on demand. Day pass: on sale once the schedule is out, no shirt.

| | Remote until 10 February | Remote from 11 February | Day pass from 3 March |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Standard** | 190 € | 240 € | 550 € |
| **Self-funded** | 90 € | 140 € | 300 € |
| **Student** | free | free | 200 € |
---
details:

#### ticket-detail ####
title: Every edition comes with its shirt
----
text:

Each three-day pass includes the shirt of its edition. Four editions, four designs.
Every edition is limited: the shirts are custom made in the exact number
sold, no reprints, no sales, no shirts at the door. Sizes are final on 31 March, no changes or
additions after that.
#### ticket-detail ####
title: Our promise
----
text:

No ticket in this shop will ever be sold cheaper than the one before it. Prices step up on
published dates and quotas. There are no promo codes and no last-minute offers. The earlier
you buy, the more you trust us and the less you pay.
#### ticket-detail ####
title: Masterclasses
----
text:

Monday, 19 April, small groups. Full-day classes run 9:00–16:00 with a one-hour lunch break at 12:00; half-day classes run 9:00–12:00 or 13:00–16:00. The [first masterclasses](/masterclasses/) are online, more will follow.

- **Full-day:** 590 € until 10 February, 690 € until 2 March, 790 € from 3 March.
- **Half-day:** 390 € until 10 February, 490 € until 2 March, 590 € from 3 March.
#### ticket-detail ####
title: Good to know
----
text:

- Free refund until 2 April, any ticket.
- Masterclasses: switch classes until 2 April, see the [FAQ](/faqs/#switch-masterclass). Cancellations follow the [masterclass terms](/terms/) (German).
- Edition I: up to five tickets per order.
- Got your talk accepted after buying a ticket? We refund it, and you keep your edition and shirt. Same for volunteers and organizers.
- Teams of five or more: contact sponsoring for the [Silver package](/sponsoring/).
- Questions: [contact form](/contact/).
